#
# object     MatMatProtocol::GetSubMatShape minimises
#              cost = (sent_ct + response_ct) * 1000 + num_automorph * 1 + num_ct_mul * 0.1
#            (memory not priced). FFN up-projection (128 x 768 x 3072) -> sub-shape (128, 64, 1):
#            12 ciphertexts sent, weight side encoded into 12 x 3072 = 36,864 plaintexts of 8192
#            coefficients carrying 64 values (128x blow-up), 36,864 x 196,608 B = 7.25 GB per matmul.
#            Predicted before the run; measured pool 8639.0 MB.
# lever      deferred materialisation. cheetah_dot.cc:352 sizes std::vector<RLWEPt> plain_mat(is_self_lhs
#            ? lhs_n : rhs_n) for the whole side, filled by one EncodeRHS before Compute. DoCompute walks
#            outer blocks, each output block accumulates over the inner index only: encode, use and
#            drop one outer slice at a time. Slice budget 256 MiB of resident plaintext, hardcoded
#            (not env-gated).
# peak       SEAL pool retains freed memory; peak = pool high-water (b0 trace: 15.09 GB by layer 0's
#            FFN, 15.34 GB after 12 layers). Deferral lowers the high-water.
# cost       same encodes, NTTs and multiplications; only interleaving changes (receive no longer
#            overlaps the encode). Typed against the wall spread.
# gate       each out[i,k] still accumulates over ascending j; encoding deterministic; COMM| unchanged.
#            Expected bit-identical.
# skips      none: BasicOTProtocols 5152.2 MB (depth 1: yacl::Buffer 6365.1 MB) is smaller; threads x 2
#            adapters x 160 MiB Ferret buffer, no free fix (thread count pinned, LPN a security trade;
#            off-path.md).
